  "projectUrl": "https://www.fieldcure.com/",
  "published": "2026-07-02T12:57:57.6Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.13.0 — DRT (Tikhonov) high-frequency inductance handling reworked; no new tools (44). drt_tikhonov's include_stray_impedance bool is replaced by a single mutually-exclusive inductance_handling choice: 'none' (RC-only), 'stray' (Löwner de-embedding), or 'gdrt' — which re-exposes Generalized DRT, fitting an RL (inductive) distribution alongside RC for distributed inductive processes. 'stray' now de-embeds the FULL inductive stray — series Ls + parallel Rp|Lp + Rx|Lx — before the fit and adds exactly that back to the reconstruction (Rs is left to the DRT fit), correcting the high-frequency reconstruction on data whose stray is (or collapses to) a series Ls or carries a second R|L branch: the add-back previously restored only Rp|Lp and dropped the Rx|Lx it had subtracted, and the series Ls was never removed. drt_tikhonov and get_analysis now report the resolved series/stray impedance for a stray run (strayValues: Rs the fitted intercept, plus the de-embedded Ls / Rp|Lp / Rx|Lx) and the inductance mode, matching the app's Results panel. Behaviour flows from the shared ZStudio engine; the parallel-stray math is unified in one place so subtract, add-back, and the inductive-free basis cannot drift.",
